Room: extension install prompts of Room profiles go to the host.

Chrome draws an extension's install confirmation (the Web Store's "Add to
Chrome", a CRX opened by the user, a re-enable after new permissions) as a
Views dialog parented to the tab or window. A Room profile's installs belong
to the host's consent sheet (the Engine protocol's willInstall with the
permission list), which answers ACCEPTED or USER_CANCELED on the same
DoneCallback.

No existing hook: the Web Store's webstorePrivate creates its prompt through
ExtensionsBrowserClient::CreateInstallPrompt and ExtensionInstallPrompt shows
it through GetDefaultShowDialogCallback(), a static that this Views file
defines; the only override is ScopedTestDialogAutoConfirm, which answers
without asking anyone. //room takes the prompt only for profiles whose host
delegate answers installs; everything else keeps Chrome's dialog.

Phase 3.6a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_extensions.mm.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/extensions/extension_install_dialog_view.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/extensions/extension_install_dialog_view.cc
index 54678ae0bd029..ac8bf93675592 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/extensions/extension_install_dialog_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/extensions/extension_install_dialog_view.cc
@@ -62,6 +62,16 @@ using content::OpenURLParams;
 using content::Referrer;
 using extensions::InstallPromptData;
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core at startup. Takes the install prompt of a profile
+// whose host answers extension installs (Room's consent sheet) and returns
+// true; false leaves the arguments untouched for Chrome's dialog.
+bool (*g_show_extension_install_dialog_hook)(
+    std::unique_ptr<ExtensionInstallPromptShowParams>&,
+    ExtensionInstallPrompt::DoneCallback&,
+    std::unique_ptr<InstallPromptData>&) = nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 namespace {
 
 // Time delay before the install button is enabled after initial display.
@@ -85,6 +95,11 @@ void ShowExtensionInstallDialogImpl(
     ExtensionInstallPrompt::DoneCallback done_callback,
     std::unique_ptr<InstallPromptData> prompt) {
   DCHECK_CURRENTLY_ON(content::BrowserThread::UI);
+  if (room::g_show_extension_install_dialog_hook &&
+      room::g_show_extension_install_dialog_hook(show_params, done_callback,
+                                                 prompt)) {
+    return;
+  }
 
   // If the dialog has to be parented to WebContents, force activate the
   // contents. See crbug.com/40059470.
